Imperial Palace of Fanazaki{offset0}







Wow, what a victory {name}! The capture of Goziya's HQ allowed us to bring to light documents proving that the Katzar invasion was in reality a huge conspiracy organized by Admiral Goziya, currently awaiting trial in prison.{pause} 

{ia16}{jail}{offset105}His diabolical plan foresaw removing the Imperial Fleet into the open sea for so-called manoeuvres, letting the Paranos land on the Emperor's loyal fiefs. Once chaos set in, Goziya was to return to the city as a liberator, miraculously provoking a Katzar retreat. By this make-believe triumph he could seize the imperial throne and condemn the emperor for incompetence. In exchange Goziya the 1st was to cede to Katzarin control over the Sakarin Islands.{offset0}


Obviously that wasn't taking into account my operation {arialbld}TSUNAMI!{arial}



Hum, hum! I don't know why I'm telling you all this {rank}, your mission is far from over.

Katzars in retreat have a deplorable habit of burning everything in their wake. {arialbld}Mekano{arial} found out the hard way. Go there and save everything you can. The Paranos are currently approaching the ancestral city of {arialbld}Kaïtan{arial}, some of the cherry trees there are hundreds of years old. The city is only defended by women and elders. It would be appropriate that your units station there BEFORE the Katzars' arrival.

Close your eyes!{pause}













